{"id":"n2-104","title":"～ないではいられない","romaji":"〜nai de wa irarenai","jlptLevel":2,"shortExplanation":"Cannot help but; cannot avoid; unable to refrain from.","longExplanation":"The ～ないではいられない grammar point is used to express a strong feeling, urge, or uncontrollable action that someone cannot resist or help doing, even if it may be undesirable. It can be translated as 'cannot help but', 'cannot avoid', or 'unable to refrain from' in English.","formation":"Verb-ない form + ではいられない or じゃいられない","examples":[{"jp":"この映画はとても感動的で、泣かないではいられなかった。","romaji":"Kono eiga wa totemo kandouteki de, nakanai de wa irarenakatta.","en":"This movie was so touching, I couldn't help but cry.","words":[{"surface":"この","vocabId":null},{"surface":"映画","vocabId":"1173720","reading":"えいが"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"とても","vocabId":null},{"surface":"感動","vocabId":"1212570","reading":"かんどう"},{"surface":"的","vocabId":"1437260","reading":"てき"},{"surface":"で","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"だ"},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"泣か","vocabId":"1229840","reading":"なく","baseForm":"泣く"},{"surface":"ない","vocabId":null},{"surface":"で","vocabId":null},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"い","vocabId":"1158500","reading":"い","baseForm":"いる"},{"surface":"られ","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"られる"},{"surface":"なかっ","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"ない"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[10,11,12,13,14]},{"jp":"彼女の笑顔を見ると、笑わないではいられない。","romaji":"Kanojo no egao wo miru to, warawanai de wa irarenai.","en":"When I see her smile, I can't help but laugh.","words":[{"surface":"彼女","vocabId":"1483150","reading":"かのじょ"},{"surface":"の","vocabId":null},{"surface":"笑顔","vocabId":"1351400","reading":"えがお"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"見る","vocabId":"1259290","reading":"みる"},{"surface":"と","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"笑わ","vocabId":"1351360","reading":"わらう","baseForm":"笑う"},{"surface":"ない","vocabId":null},{"surface":"で",